{
 "schema": "intract-features models.lock v1",
 "read": "3 November 2026",
 "conventions": [
  "Entries sit under 'models', keyed as the stage configs name them; readers accept that table (segment/sat.py resolve_pinned_snapshot, parse.model_pin).",
  "'files' lists what the consuming stage verifies by SHA-256 before loading, in the folder it resolves: the entry's 'path', else the folder an INTRACT_* variable names, else the Hugging Face cache snapshot of 'revision' under HF_HUB_CACHE.",
  "A 'conversion' entry is loaded from $INTRACT_MODELS/<conversion.dir>, which jobs/arc/staging.py convert builds from 'hub_files' in j0_build. A SHA-256 of null is pending: no stage loads such a file until jobs/arc/staging.py run-config writes a run's config with the hash recorded by that conversion and the entry's 'path'; the hash is then transcribed here from records/.",
  "No ARC path is written here; jobs/arc/env.sh defines HF_HUB_CACHE, STANZA_RESOURCES_DIR, INTRACT_MODELS and the other folders.",
  "Revisions are full commits; nothing is fetched by branch name. 'hub_ref_main' marks a snapshot that third-party code loads by name offline, so refs/main must name 'revision'.",
  "An entry marked 'optional' is read by no stage and is staged only on request (jobs/arc/staging.py models --include-optional, or --only naming it), since its conversion costs disk, memory and hours."
 ],
